    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-038: Pseudo-Class Expansion** — 14 new pseudo-classes across three CSS categories. **Spec documents an honest scope amendment**: the original title was \"Structural pseudo-classes,\" but measurement showed structural is the *lowest*-value category on Wikipedia.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation lands in a follow-up PR (3 commits: structural, logical, lang + docs).\n\n## The measurement that expanded the scope\n\nCensus of pseudo-class usage across Wikipedia's CSS:\n\n| Category | Pseudo | Uses |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Language** | `:lang(...)` | **410** |\n| **Logical** | `:not(...)` | **374** |\n| **Logical** | `:where(...)` | 16 |\n| **Logical** | `:is(...)` | 2 |\n| **Structural** | `:last-child` | 13 |\n| **Structural** | `:first-child` | 12 |\n| **Structural** | `:first-of-type` | 6 |\n| **Structural** | `:empty` | 3 |\n| **Structural** | `:only-child` | 2 |\n| **Structural** | `:last-of-type` | 2 |\n| **Relative** (deferred) | `:has(...)` | 8 |\n| **Direction** (deferred) | `:dir(...)` | 1 |\n\n**`:nth-child()` — the headline feature of the original structural-only scope — has zero uses in Wikipedia's CSS.** Structural-only would unlock ~38 rules. Structural + logical + language unlocks **~840**.\n\n## The scope amendment\n\nDocumented in the ADR (preserved alongside the original \"structural\" title in Context — same pattern as ADR-034's SVG amendment):\n\n### Structural (10 pseudos)\n\n`:first-child`, `:last-child`, `:only-child`, `:nth-child(An+B)`, `:nth-last-child(An+B)`, `:first-of-type`, `:last-of-type`, `:only-of-type`, `:nth-of-type(An+B)`, `:nth-last-of-type(An+B)`, `:empty`\n\nComplete CSS Selectors L3 §6.6 category, including the 6 forms that appear zero times in Wikipedia (spec completeness).\n\n### Logical (3 pseudos)\n\n`:not()`, `:is()`, `:where()` — compound-arg comma lists. `:not()` covers 374 uses across 100% simple/attr/pseudo args (compound args ship for spec completeness; combinators deferred).\n\n### Language (1 pseudo)\n\n`:lang(tag)` — 410 uses. Walks ancestor chain for `lang` attribute, prefix-matches BCP-47 tags (`en` matches `en-US`, but not vice versa).\n\n## Specificity handling\n\n| Pseudo | Specificity |\n|---|---|\n| Structural | `0,1,0` |\n| `:not(S)` | max of argument specificities (CSS4) |\n| `:is(S1,...)` | max of argument specificities |\n| `:where(...)` | **`0,0,0` always** — this is the whole point |\n| `:lang()` | `0,1,0` |\n\nThe `:where()` zero-specificity is critical: it's how `:where(:not([role='button']))` applies color/font resets that any class selector can override.\n\n## What stays deferred\n\n- **`:has()`** — 8 uses, needs descendant traversal (different complexity class from sibling-index reads)\n- **`:dir()`** — 1 use, inside `:has()`, same dependency\n- **Combinator args inside `:not()` / `:is()` / `:where()`** — 0 uses; CSS4 drops individual entries from lists\n- **Form-state pseudos** (`:focus`, `:active`, `:checked`, `:enabled`, `:disabled`, `:read-only`, `:focus-visible`, `:placeholder`) — separate category, own ADR\n- **`:nth-child(An+B of S)`**, `:nth-col`, `:scope` — zero uses\n\n## Expected visible delta\n\n| Source | Rules | Expected first-viewport delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| Structural | 38 | Small (spacing/separator rules) |\n| `:not()` | 374 | Moderate (theme/state rules apply) |\n| `:is()` / `:where()` | 18 | Minor |\n| `:lang()` | 410 | **Zero on English Wikipedia** (infrastructure for non-English) |\n| **Total** | **~840** | **Small-positive, measured in impl Commit 3** |\n\n## Test plan\n\n~20-25 tests in `[css][pseudos][adr-038]`:\n\n- Structural: all 10 forms, An+B grammar (odd/even/N/An/An±M/-An±M), `:empty` whitespace handling, same-type vs all-sibling distinction\n- Logical: `:not()` inverts, compound args, `:is()` matches either, `:where()` zero specificity\n- Language: exact match, prefix match, no-overreach, no-lang-anywhere\n- Specificity: `:not(.a)` contributes `.a`'s, `:is(.a, #b)` contributes `#b`'s, `:where(.a)` contributes 0\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Scope amendment accepted** — structural title preserved in Context, expanded scope documented in amendment section\n- [ ] **`:nth-child()` zero-uses justification** — ships for CSS spec completeness, ~50 lines, category completion\n- [ ] **`:not()` compound args accepted** — zero observed uses, ships because the sub-parser for `:is()` already handles compounds; rejecting from `:not()` would be arbitrary\n- [ ] **`:lang()` zero-visible-delta on English page** — honest about what ships vs. what's demonstrable\n- [ ] **`:has()` deferral accepted** — different complexity class (descendant vs. sibling)\n- [ ] **`:where()` zero specificity** — the specific reason it exists, tested explicitly\n\nRefs #194\n",
